zreader bench105 (for 0.10.4)

Install (on the Kindle, over SSH):
  mkdir -p /mnt/us/zreader && cd /mnt/us/zreader && tar -xzf /mnt/us/bench105.tgz
Run while zreader is NOT running:
  sh /mnt/us/zreader/bench/zrbench.sh -l /mnt/us/documents scan-b memory .epub

Each BOOK is a path or a case-insensitive name searched in /mnt/us/documents and
/mnt/us/Books. -l sets the folder used for the library test (default /mnt/us/Books).
Takes roughly 2-4 minutes per book plus about 1 minute for the library test.

What it measures
  zrbench book (the reader's own render code, headless):
    open_cold / open_warm, open_to_first_page, render p50/p95/max over 30 pages
    (pages 11-40 with the reader's PDF fit-page + trim + clean-scan settings, EPUB at
    the default text settings), rerender (display list cached), a prerender model
    (2 workers, 2 pages ahead, turns every 0.7 s and 0.25 s: hit % and wait), peak RSS.
  zreader --sim (the installed reader, headless: no /dev/fb0, no touch input, no
    governor/light/Wi-Fi/Amazon-UI changes): cold open with empty caches + 30 turns at
    0.7 s, warm reopen + 30 turns at 0.25 s; first frame, touch-up->complete p50/p90
    (about 1 ms = page was prerendered; a miss shows the render time), worker render
    times, reader peak RSS (VmHWM sampled every 0.2 s).
  Library: scan time and time until the last cover batch, cold and cached.
  Dictionary: English (WordNet) and Latin lookup times, first lookup and p50/p95/max.

Safety: all reader data (state, notes, caches, thumbnails) goes to a temporary folder
under bench/ that is deleted at the end. /mnt/us/zreader state, notes and settings are
never read or written. The CPU governor is set to performance for the run, as the
reader does while rendering, and restored at exit; powerd is kept awake
(preventScreenSaver 1, back to 0 at exit). Both are printed. bench105 also compares
MuPDF -O2 (zrbench-o2) with the shipped -Os build: pixel hash and render time.
Report: printed and saved as /mnt/us/zreader/bench/report-DATE.txt.

Build (from the repository root, after ./build-mupdf.sh):
  zig cc -target arm-linux-musleabihf -mcpu=cortex_a53 -O2 -I src -I tools/bench -I MUPDF/include \
    tools/bench/zrbench.c src/render.c src/dictionary.c src/latin.c \
    MUPDF/build/armhf-release/libmupdf.a MUPDF/build/armhf-release/libmupdf-third.a \
    -static -lpthread -lm -s -o bench/zrbench
then copy zrbench, zrbench.sh and this README to /mnt/us/zreader/bench/ on the Kindle.
zrbench-o2 is the same build against MuPDF built with OPT=-O2 (optional).
hyph_la.h holds the reader's compact Latin hyphenation patterns (from src/hyph/la).
